Subject: Cantor Prototype Graduation and Reflection Loop P0 Explosion

@ [explosion_uuid] 112d29ff-7a7e-46dd-b5da-612ebe99e720
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_prototype_graduation_reflection_loop\Source_Document_Manifest.sop

& [Fold1Intent] is high-leverage formation before breadth
  + select the smallest novel identity whose execution tests the architecture
  + preserve user dictation before interpretation
  + reject repository-wide maturity as the entry condition for one reversible experiment

& [Fold2Graduation] is specification transformed through visible stages
  + source becomes a feature flowchart with descriptions
  + feature flowchart becomes typed data and an executable control flow
  + executable flow becomes a bounded implementation slice
  + implementation becomes evidence before any promotion decision

& [Fold3PrototypeSubject] is the real two-pass Cantor reflection loop
  + a user stimulus enters llama.cpp
  + the model emits one structured route_attention call
  + the host validates and invokes the existing Cantor MCP adapter
  + the adapter returns a verified AttentionFrame or an explicit refusal
  + a second llama.cpp pass reflects over that result and emits final structured output
  + a control run demonstrates the no-tool boundary

& [Fold4Data] is inspectable external state
  + Stimulus is immutable caller text
  + InferenceRequest records one provider request
  + SubroutineCall records the selected name call identity and arguments
  + SubroutineResult records structured MCP success or fault without authority promotion
  + ReflectionRequest records the exact evidence supplied to pass two
  + FinalOutput records a schema-checked model conclusion
  + ExecutionTrace records transitions timings sanitized provider messages and faults

& [Fold5SecurityHonesty] is representation integrity rather than omniscience
  + exact tool name argument shape call count and transition order are enforced by the host
  + learned routing remains a learned evidence-backed proposal
  + tool refusal remains visible to the second pass and final output
  + malformed unavailable or contradictory boundaries fail closed
  + provider-private reasoning is excluded from durable evidence

& [Fold6Faults] is the falsification surface
  + direct_answer_without_required_call
  + wrong_tool
  + malformed_arguments
  + multiple_tool_calls
  + mcp_unavailable
  + mcp_protocol_fault
  + result_shape_fault
  + second_pass_tool_loop
  + final_schema_fault
  + refusal_omission
  + provider_unavailable
  + trace_write_fault

& [Fold7PhaseLock] is an experimental P0 waist
  + inside is one model one read-only tool at most one tool call exactly two provider passes for routed cases one process-local trace and three acceptance cases
  + outside is nested calls dynamic procedures persistent stacks autonomous effects GUI llama.cpp modification hidden-state access shared inference model training and trusted-catalogue admission
  + [exhaustion_state] is seven_fold_phase_locked_for_reversible_prototype

& [Pruning] preserves speed without semantic collapse
  + reuse the existing llama.cpp tool-call seam rather than rebuild provider transport
  + reuse the live route_attention MCP contract rather than simulate Cantor
  + use compact response_mode frame for positive routing
  + keep proof-rich refusal intact
  + defer reusable engine extraction until the live loop passes
